{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Though</b> — Because the place of the sun's elevation moves from one degree to another and from one zodiacal sign to another, therefore the astrologers said that a time will come when the dry land will turn into sea and the sea into dry land. Afterward they said that the meaning is, were it so — even though it will not be — for HaShem set a boundary for the waters that they shall not return to cover the earth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:58.739000456Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}